# Context for Claude (example)

This is my private setup, without the personal parts. I don't read these files: I talk with
Claude in chat and see the result on my calendar. The repo is there so Claude always has the
right context and gets the numbers right.

## Read first

`STATO.md`: where we are, this week, open actions. One screen. If only one thing gets updated
after a conversation, it's this one.

## The map

| Where | What | When it changes |
|---|---|---|
| `STATO.md` | the present: this week, open actions, pending decisions | almost every time |
| `piani/` | what **should** happen: running, strength, the multi-sport week | when the plan changes |
| `storico/` | what **did** happen and what we learned, plus decisions | after every session analysed |
| `riferimenti/` | what is **true**: HR zones, what the watch measures, scientific sources | rarely |
| `dati/` | CSVs generated by `./aggiorna` + raw Garmin JSON | never by hand |
| `sistema/` | the scripts | when data collection changes |

History is appended, never rewritten.

## Before analysing anything

Run `./aggiorna` and look at how old the last watch sync is. "Today's" data is often stuck at
last night's sync, and reading it as fresh leads to wrong conclusions.

## Rules we don't want to rediscover

- **Use the max HR measured in a field test**, not the watch default (198 on mine) and not the
  highest value seen in training. Never quote the watch's zones.
- **The Instinct Solar gen 1 has no VO2max, Training Status/Load/Effect or Training Readiness.**
  We compute load (TRIMP → acute/chronic → ACWR) and readiness (RHR, body battery, sleep) ourselves.
- **Scientific claims are checked on the original abstract** (Europe PMC), not on a search
  snippet. One audit corrected 12 claims that had been written from snippets.
- **When the plan changes, the calendar is updated at the same moment.** An old event is worse
  than no event: on the phone it looks authoritative.
- **The watch doesn't see everything** (beach volley, for example): if I don't say it, it didn't
  happen.
